  "line": 1968,
  "title": "The MERGE_HEAD check reads only the first entry and treats a failed read as no merge",
  "detail": "The guard uses `git rev-parse -q --verify MERGE_HEAD` with allowFail. Two inconsistent states still pass it and then fail generically in prepareMerge/validateMerge, which takes the verified-draft fallback this issue removes: (1) MERGE_HEAD with pendingRebaseSha on the first line and another commit on a second line: rev-parse returns the first, the guard passes, and git would commit an octopus merge with both; (2) a MERGE_HEAD whose content isn't a full object id (abbreviated, garbage): rev-parse fails, stdout is empty, and the guard treats it as no merge in progress. Read MERGE_HEAD's contents through the hardened wrapper (`git rev-parse --git-path MERGE_HEAD`, then read the file): only a confirmed absence (the file doesn't exist) passes; otherwise require exactly one line equal to the full pendingRebaseSha; any other content or a failed read is a DeliveryHeadError. Add tests for a two-line MERGE_HEAD and an abbreviated one: both end with the delivery refusal and publish nothing."
 }
]
